# Freenove ESP32-WROVER-E (classic ESP32-D0WD, 4MB flash / 8MB PSRAM) --
# LEAN RUNTIME (full features) / portable 4WD stand-in.  partitions_4M_ota_trim
# (1.75MB dual-OTA app slots + 448KB LittleFS), same as the 4WD.
# The full test suite does NOT fit the 448KB FS all at once, so tests are run in
# SECTIONS: w3_ai_scripts/wrover_sectioned_tests.sh uploadfs's the runtime + one tier's
# test files at a time, loads that tier's runner over serial, captures, repeats.
# Own pin map: boards/pins/Freenove-ESP32-WROVER.scm (WROVER-CAM module pinout; sonar on GPIO12/13
# -- NOT the 4WD's 12/15, which collides with the SD host; the reason is in that file's header).
#   *** THOSE ARE PINS, NOT A SENSOR.  THERE IS EXACTLY ONE HC-SR04 IN THE LAB AND IT IS ON THE 4WD
#   (owner, 2026-10-07).  This board compiles the sonar feature and names pins for it; nothing is
#   wired to them, so Sonar.ping here times out forever and `have-Sonar` tells you nothing about
#   whether an echo can arrive.  The 4WD manifest says the same from the other side ("CANNOT move to
#   the WROVER, which has no sonar").  Written here because a pin map in a feature list reads as a
#   capability, which is how two sessions came to look for a second sonar board. ***
# Core module set mirrors the S3 devkit (proven to boot); no motor/LED/robot HW so
# Led/Buzzer/Motor .loop just tick empty behaviour queues (harmless).

# Core runtime
core/setup.scm
core/Compiler.scm
core/Lobs.scm
core/Behaviors.scm
core/Terminal.scm
file: boards/pins/Freenove-ESP32-WROVER.scm -> Pins.scm
core/Timers.scm
core/ESP32.scm
core/CommonIO.scm
core/Buzzer.scm
core/Sonar.scm
core/WiFi.scm
core/I2C.scm
core/Wire.scm
core/PCA9685.scm
core/PCF8574.scm
core/WS2812.scm
core/LightSensor.scm
core/LCD1602.scm
core/array.scm

# R5RS/R7RS overrides
rxrs/rxrs.scm
rxrs/rxrs_cxr.scm
rxrs/rxrs_exceptions.scm
rxrs/rxrs_continuations.scm
rxrs/rxrs_promises.scm
rxrs/rxrs_quasiquote.scm
