# Board-specific init
boards/Freenove-ESP32-WROVER.scm
# Target setup: brings the OV2640 up at the END of boot, before any user code loads.  [B608] --
# the camera needs a contiguous ~23 KB internal-DMA block and ONE extra .scm load exhausts it.
boards/setup-Freenove-ESP32-WROVER.scm

# Serial file+command tunnel: resident LLIP receiver -- host sends (llt) then op/da/cl file
# frames and/or (ev <form>) command frames; O(N) clean, no per-char REPL echo.
features/llip-serial.scm

# [P247] Promote NAMED procedures into the low-latency native pool at the end of app startup, and
# report which ones were REFUSED.  Loaded HERE and not in every manifest on purpose: a feature file
# is an application opt-in (compare features/bacnet.scm, in 2 of 26 manifests), and the set of
# deadline-critical procedures is a property of the application, not of the part.  The full scm/
# library ships in every customer package regardless of manifest, so a customer who wants it stages
# it; this line is what makes it present in THIS board's default image, where it is exercised.
# B817: it bytecode-compiles before promoting, because compile-low-latency! handed an interpreted
# procedure compiles nothing and truthfully returns #f -- which reads exactly like a full pool.
features/promote-named.scm

# P123 Part D: carry a camera frame over LLIP as BINARY (s-expression header + raw bytes).
# NOT base64 -- every LambLisp port is already a binary port, so a JPEG rides the same TCP
# connection the move programs use, unencoded.  Codec only: it loads on a board with no camera.
features/llip-vision.scm
# The vehicle half of the mini-HUD: camera frames plus sonar/drive telemetry to a panel.
# Needs the llip-vision codec above; the panel half is demos/hud-panel.scm.
demos/hud-car.scm
# [P260] THE STATIONARY RECOGNISER, which is what this board IS now (owner, 2026-10-14: "a
# non-roving animal recognizer").  It drives hud-car.scm's transport rather than reimplementing it
# and adds the part a vehicle has no use for: an arrival/departure state machine per detected
# group, so the record is "animal present 14:22:07 -> 14:22:41" and not a tally of 200 sightings.
# It loads hud-car.scm itself, so the line above is what puts the file on the FS, not what loads it.
demos/watcher.scm

# LLIP SERVER -- filesystem operations for a remote LambLisp client.  Added 2026-09-12: EVERY
# PUBLISHED TARGET SUPPORTS LLIP BY DEFAULT.  This target staged the serial RECEIVER below but not
# the SERVER, so `llip ls/send/run` against it answered nothing -- a capability the customer's own
# `tools/llip` CLI advertises, shipped half-present.  The two halves are not interchangeable:
# llip-serial.scm is the resident (llt) that accepts a serial session; llip-server.scm is what
# serves the file operations inside it.
tools/llip-server.scm

# Runtime defaults
runtime-defaults/Settings.scm
